### 1. Review of Candidate Gaps (`G1`–`G12`) in [`DRAFT.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/_review/DRAFT.md)

- **G1 — AGREE.** [`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L107) (proof-order item 4) and Phase E ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L161), `R-0482`/`R-0495`) defer functional models until Phase E, yet Phase C slices 7–18 ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L217-L228), [`EXAMPLES.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#L21-L73)) require `#[proof(path)]` user theorems. Fixing the theorem-subject shape in `A2i`/`A3` and generating pure models at slice 8 avoids raw clock-indexed Core proofs.
- **G2 — AGREE.** [`types.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/types.md#L1498-L1515) (`TYPE-22@1`) inlines every constant with no storage, [`references.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/references.md#L432) (`REF-5@3`, `REF-6@2`) only borrows locals, and [`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L227) places constants at slice 17 while crypto/EVM (slice 15) and `grep` (slice 16) need static lookup tables that do not blow the slice-0 stack bound ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L256)).
- **G3 — AGREE.** [`R4_RATIONALE.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/archive/decisions-2026-11-05/R4_RATIONALE.md#L292-L343) (`F6`) and [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L258) (`Q7.10`) omit `SIGPIPE` (silent termination on closed pipes/sockets violates Rule 18, [`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L156)), inherited file descriptors `>= 3` (ambient authority under Rule 11, [`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L110)), `umask`, `RLIMIT_STACK`, and `exit_group(134)` vs `SIGABRT`.
- **G4 — AGREE.** [`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L328) explicitly notes "Wide-integer arithmetic is unplaced", and slice 2 ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L212)) lacks primitive `rotate_left`/`right`, `clz`/`ctz`, `popcount`, `swap_bytes`, `add_with_carry`, `sub_with_borrow`, and `mul_wide` in the slice-7 constant-time table. Note: because [`types.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/types.md#L1640-L1662) refuses anonymous tuples, carry/wide ops must return named `Copy` structs, not `(sum, carry)` / `(hi, lo)`.
- **G5 — AGREE.** [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L846-L864) (`decided-project-infoflow-2026-11-06`) and [`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L98-L107) (`C7`) make scalar `Secret<T>` `Copy`, wipe only linear secret arrays/allocations on destroy, and make `abort()` skip cleanup (`OD10`). Rule 12 ([`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L116)) requires stating stack-move, spill, frame, and abort residue in the slice-7/15/19 claim scope.
- **G6 — AGREE.** [`ffi.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#L202-L235) (`FFI-5`) and `R-0556` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L496)) generate `.coni` interfaces, and `R-0301` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L499)) checks ABI layout generally, but nothing emits `.h` headers from exports (Rule 5, [`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L68)), generates reviewed Concrete `extern fn` bindings from C headers, or checks per-declaration C layout against `clang` at slice 25.
- **G7 — AGREE.** Inline assembly is not listed in [`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L260-L404) ("What Concrete refuses") or [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md). Explicitly refusing inline assembly—even inside `trusted` blocks—and requiring foreign assembly to cross the slice-25 `extern fn` boundary with named premises protects the Core semantics and both backends.
- **G8 — DISAGREE.** Reopens decided showcase placement: [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L931-L956) (`decided-2026-11-07-showcases`, `decided-2026-11-07-final-slices`) and [`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L238) explicitly decided that slice 27's web server is sequential (one connection at a time) and that the encrypted tunnel and concurrent server wait until after slice 28 and the randomness/nonce audit.
- **G9 — AGREE.** `OD62` ([`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L1352)) only refuses unused bindings inside a function body, and [`modules.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/modules.md#L1-L532) (`MOD-1`–`MOD-9`) has no rule refusing unused imports or unreachable private module items at slice 17.
- **G10 — AGREE.** `R-0603` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L415)) puts `spec_version` in compiler reports and `R-0589` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L466), [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L801-L816)) versions `[policy]`/`[assumptions]` in `Concrete.toml`, but nothing in `Concrete.toml` records the language `spec_version` a package requires at slice 17.
- **G11 — DISAGREE.** Already covered by `R-0599` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L464), [`SPARK.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/SPARK.md#L204-L229)) and `R-0462 -> R-0259` ([`IDEAS.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/IDEAS.md#L74)). Moreover, running `spec fn` on native backends violates [`contracts.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/contracts.md#L290) (`CON-5@2`: `spec fn` is erased; no code is generated) and [`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L397), and `#[test]` takes no parameters (`OD146`, [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L1436)).
- **G12 — DISAGREE.** Already covered and dispositioned: binary-format DSLs are tracked as `R-0406` (`DEFERRED`) in [`IDEAS.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/IDEAS.md#L97), and external source generators whose output is reviewed as ordinary source are already established in [`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L360-L361).

**Ranking adjustment:** Drop `G8`, `G11`, and `G12`. Promote `G4` ahead of `G3` because slice 2 (`mul_wide`, bit ops) and slice 15 (`u256`) sit on the critical path earlier than hosted I/O slices 16/18/27, and promote `G9` ahead of `G6` (slice 17 vs slice 25): **`G1, G2, G4, G3, G5, G9, G6, G7, G10`**.

