### 3. Missed Gaps (Passing the [`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L211-L258) Admission Test)

#### M1. Disjoint mutable subview splitting (`split_at`) (`disjoint-subview-split`)
- **Sources**: Rust `slice::split_at_mut`, SPARK/Ada unconstrained array slice partitioning, Low* `Buffer.sub` disjointness, Hylo subscript projections.
- **Problem**: By `OD15(a)` ([`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L1305)) and Foundation `C5` ([`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L78)), Concrete enforces **whole-root** borrow conflict: opening a mutable subview (`borrow mut a from l until r as v`, [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L220-L221) `Q3.2`–`Q3.4`) freezes the entire root `a`. Safe code therefore cannot hold two disjoint mutable subviews of the same array or `HeapArray` at once (needed for in-place block crypto at slice 15, LZ77/DEFLATE window-to-output copying in PNG at slice 21–22, and divide-and-conquer algorithms).
- **Proposed slice**: **Slice 15** (arrays) and **Slice 21** (`HeapArray`): a scoped split form (or primitive) that binds two second-class mutable views `[0, mid)` and `[mid, len)` under the single root freeze when `mid <= len` (discharged by the octagon domain `R-0584` or an `else` branch).
- **Why not already covered**: `swap_at` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L225), `Q3.2`) swaps two single elements; `Q3.3`–`Q3.4` (`borrow [mut] a from l until r as v`) produces only *one* subview while freezing the root.

#### M2. Proved bulk view primitives (`copy_from`, `copy_within`, `fill`) (`bulk-view-copy-fill`)
- **Sources**: Rust `slice::copy_from_slice` / `copy_within` / `fill`, Zig `@memcpy` / `@memset`, Ada array slice assignment (overlap-safe).
- **Problem**: Because whole-root conflict (`OD15(a)`, `C5`) forbids borrowing a source subrange and a destination subrange of the same buffer simultaneously, safe code cannot pass two subviews of one buffer to a copy helper, forcing element-by-element index loops for sliding windows (`grep` at slice 16–18, DEFLATE in PNG at slice 21–22, HTTP buffer compaction at slice 27). Hand-rolled loops obscure bulk sequence updates in Lean proofs (`G1`) and prevent proved lowering to `memcpy`/`memmove`/`memset`.
- **Proposed slice**: **Slice 15** (arrays/views): total primitives `fill`, `copy_from` (distinct views, equal length), and `copy_within` (overlapping ranges within one `&mut [T; ..]`), with octagon bounds obligations and a single list/array range-update equation in `C4`/`C9`.
- **Why not already covered**: Slice 15 ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L225)) lists only `get`, `set`, `swap_at`, and single-range subviews (`Q3.2`–`Q3.4`).

#### M3. Bit-exact IEEE-754 floating-point determinism contract (`ieee754-float-determinism`)
- **Sources**: WebAssembly deterministic IEEE-754 specification (canonical NaNs, no implicit FMA), CompCert `Flocq` (verified IEEE-754 in Coq), SPARK bounded float axioms.
- **Problem**: From slice 0, CI requires **exact observation agreement** across the Lean reference evaluator, LLVM, and LCB (`R-0578`, [`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L448)), and slice 26 adds `f32`/`f64` for the Wasm sandbox showcase ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L236, #L275)). Without forbidding implicit FMA contraction, fixing the hardware rounding/denormal mode (`MXCSR`/`FPCR`) at startup, and canonicalizing NaN payloads (observable via `reinterpret`, `OD99`), LLVM, LCB, and the Lean evaluator will diverge on legal programs.
- **Proposed slice**: **Slice 26** (and launcher FPU control-word setup in the `Q7.10` target table): specify round-to-nearest-even, no FTZ/DAZ, no implicit FMA contraction, canonical quiet NaN bits on arithmetic, and explicit status of `x / 0.0` under Rule 18.
- **Why not already covered**: Foundation `C2` ([`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L40)) explicitly notes *"The interface admits float instances but does not invent their unsettled details,"* and `OD63`/`OD99`/`OD107` only cover `!==` on `NaN`, `reinterpret`, and float-to-int conversions.

#### M4. Incoming FFI contract for exported Concrete functions (`#[export_name]`) (`export-fn-abi-authority-contract`)
- **Sources**: CompCertO incoming call interfaces ([`INFLUENCES.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/project/INFLUENCES.md#L586)), Rust `extern "C" fn` unwind boundary, Ada `Pragma Export`, Wasm Component Model exported functions.
- **Problem**: [`ffi.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#L204) (`FFI-5`) allows exporting Concrete functions to C via `#[export_name]`, but `FFI-3` ([`ffi.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#L71)) only restricts `extern fn` (outgoing calls to C). Nothing specifies for an `#[export_name]` function: (a) that its signature is restricted to FFI-safe types and emitted with the platform C calling convention (`FFI-11`), (b) how `with(...)` capabilities and linear grant values behave when called by foreign C code that cannot forge Concrete grants (Rule 11), and (c) the foreign caller's stack/argument validity premises in the audit report.
- **Proposed slice**: **Slice 25** (and Foundation `C10` `Frame`): enforce `FFI-3` type safety and C ABI on `#[export_name]` functions, forbid unforgeable operational grants in their signatures unless passed via an opaque linear handle, and record foreign-caller entry premises in `[assumptions]`.
- **Why not already covered**: `FFI-5` ([`ffi.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#L204-L235)) only checks symbol-name collisions and module visibility.

#### M5. `sizeof::<T>()` and `alignof::<T>()` in the `Q6.2` statically-known value table (`static-sizeof-alignof-known`)
- **Sources**: C11 `_Static_assert`, Zig `comptime` layout checks, Rust `const { assert!(size_of::<T>() == N) }`, Ada representation clause checks.
- **Problem**: [`ffi.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#L272) (`FFI-7`) defines `sizeof::<T>()` and `alignof::<T>()`, and Foundation `C3`/`C4` ([`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L46-L63)) makes layout a pure function of the target profile. However, `Q6.2`'s closed list of statically-known expressions ([`R4_RATIONALE.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/archive/decisions-2026-11-05/R4_RATIONALE.md#L477-L494)) excludes `sizeof::<T>()` and `alignof::<T>()` ("any other call ... known? no"). As a result, constant initializers (`Q6.4`) and compile-time `assert`s cannot use `sizeof::<T>()` to size buffers or statically verify wire/FFI struct sizes.
- **Proposed slice**: **Slice 9 / 17 / 25**: include `sizeof::<T>()` and `alignof::<T>()` for concrete `T` in `Q6.2`'s closed statically-known expression grammar.
- **Why not already covered**: `R-0284` (`DEFERRED` in [`IDEAS.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/IDEAS.md#L92)) is about pointer alignment facts for SIMD, not `sizeof`/`alignof` in `Q6.2`.

ANSWER: AGREE=G1,G2,G3,G4,G5,G6,G7,G9,G10; DISAGREE=G8,G11,G12; MISSED=disjoint-subview-split,bulk-view-copy-fill,ieee754-float-determinism,export-fn-abi-authority-contract,static-sizeof-alignof-known
